{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thanks for checking before acting. This email is not legitimate. It came from a lookalike address (it-support@brightIine-help.example, with a capital I in place of the lowercase l), and our mail filter already caught it and holds it as phishing in your quarantine. Please don't click any links, reply to it, or forward it to colleagues. Leave it where it is so the security team can review it. Payroll sign-in is not affected by this message. If you already clicked a link or typed your password into anything after receiving it, tell us right away so we can act quickly. Please don't ignore that step. Someone from the team is looking into the sender and will block it for everyone if needed. For payroll questions, use the official payroll contact, not links in email.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket EVAL-email-05 (Aisha Khan, user 5, HR Generalist, active, not VIP, no failed logins, password last set 2026-09-11, device BL-LT-0105). Checked quarantine per KB-008: message Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example, subject 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', classed as phishing, not releasable. Lookalike domain uses capital I instead of l, so it impersonates IT. Did not attempt release (phishing, and the tool would refuse). Also in quarantine: Q-1001 and Q-1002, both spam and unrelated. The message reached the user's quarantine, so the user received it. Not confirmed whether she clicked or entered credentials; reply asks her to report immediately. Per KB-008, escalating for security review. Please check whether other users received the same message (same lookalike sender) and consider blocking the domain. If the user reports any click or password entry, follow KB-029 (sign-in review, block, reset) immediately.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008",
    "KB-029"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
